<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratanpur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratanpur is a town in the Bilaspur district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Founded in the 11th century by Ratnaraja I of the Kalachuri dynasty, it became the capital of the Kalachuris of Ratanpur, who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakshina-kosala">Dakshina Kosala</a> for centuries, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a> took it in 1741. Its many temples and tanks include the Mahamaya temple, a major pilgrimage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ratanpur.jpg" alt="Ratanpur" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prithwiraj Dhang · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SculpturesFort_Ratanpur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
